WEBVTT

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.240
The place is Abenobashi Shopping Arcade, Osaka.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.990
It's a nice shopping arcade with real human warmth...

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.290
...but well, it hasn't been able to resist the passage of time...

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.770
...and one shop after another has gone out of business like teeth falling out of a comb.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.330
The whole place is turning into open lots. It's so sad.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.770
And that's where Sasshi and Arumi were born and raised.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.210
Twelve years have passed since they've formed their duo.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.590
But the time to say good-bye has a way of coming around.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.930
Arumi's family is going to move to Lake Akan in Hokkaido.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.570
Sad little Sasshi.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.540
And this is the story of their last summer break in grade school.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.890
The two have jumped, you see.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:07.920
Where, you ask?

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.120
Well, the thing is, it's a world that doesn't make a whole lot of sense.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:26.910
I wonder, is this the new department store that Mom was talking about?

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.740
Where the heck would you find such a confusing department store?

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.830
It's gotta be a foreign castle, no matter how ya look at it.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.780
Foreign? Like where?

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.950
Foreign means Europe, of course! What're ya talking about?

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.550
How can ya peg it like that?

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.680
'Sides, talk about broad. Europe!

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.090
Maybe it's French?

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:45.460
It's French! It's gotta be!

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.690
So, like I said, how can ya peg it like that?!

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.610
Have ya ever heard of any rumors...

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.740
...that there're still some dragons surviving in France?

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.940
Like hell I would've.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.310
I know! Cell phone!

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.380
How long're ya gonna stay leaned up against me?!

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.900
Cell phone! Cell phone!

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.440
That's right!

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.040
Shoot, there's no signal.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.420
Which means, this really is France.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.260
If it's France, we're in deep trouble.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.860
We won't even be able to order food.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.160
Arumi, can you order a Meal A or something in French?

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.130
Even if I could, I wouldn't!

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.960
Never mind 'bout that. You got money?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.440
Money?!

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.800
Money... Money...

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.940
There we go!

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.540
Man, I'm beat.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.220
It was speaking in Japanese.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.220
It said, "Man, I'm beat."

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.950
Looks like we can understand the language here.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.310
What the heck? It's your papa.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.350
Dad!

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.100
Oh, call me "Papa"!

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.520
Your stomach hurting or something, Dad?

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.810
Non, non, "Papa".

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.510
No, never mind the "non, non".

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.350
Won't you tell us what the heck is going on around here, Dad?

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:24.110
Look, look, repeat after me. "Papa."

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.490
That was English in the middle for some reason.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.950
Papa!

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.950
Bon jour, in a sense, mon amour.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.120
Oh, Sir Hero!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.390
Hero?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.130
Hi, Sir Hero.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.960
Aki-nee!

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.440
Aki-nee is...

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.110
Good luck defeating the Great Evil Lord!

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.010
Here's some war funds for you.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.980
800 gold pieces!

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.310
War funds?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.060
War?! What do you mean, war?! And what's this Great Evil Lord?!

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.690
"Summoned and I pop out, ta-da!"

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.040
They're all weird shops, but...

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.000
Say, Sasshi, doesn't it sorta feel familiar?

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.270
Feel familiar?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.750
What's this?

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.280
Spot!

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.440
C'mere, Spot! Spot! Spot!

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.390
That was hot!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.130
Why's it Spot?

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.500
Little critters with pointy ears are usually "Spot"!

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.100
Ain't that right?!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.330
Or you like John better?!

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.700
Man, you're so annoying.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.360
Who's the more annoying one here?!

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.880
This is the pits, for real.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.080
Is this some kinda curse too?

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.590
This is stupid.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.080
To hell with it, you blithering idiot!

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.090
Here's your change! Fifty billion gold pieces!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.420
I've heard that voice somewhere before!

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.920
Go build a house with it or something!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.930
Hey, it's you, Kouhei-san!

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.030
Eh?! What the?! You're a hero I haven't seen before!

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.600
To hell with it!

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.190
Kouhei-san, the down home Tokyo version.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.880
You blithering idiot!

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.140
Hurry up and buy some equipment, you retards!

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:25.510
Excuse me, what's this place called?

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.240
What did you say, you damned blithering idiots?!

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.210
This is Abenobashi Shopping Arcade!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.700
Abenobashi Shopping Arcade?!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.630
It's a bastard sword!

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.150
A bladesword?!

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.730
They've even got the Muramasa blade!

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.820
Sasshi, keep it to one item. You shouldn't waste your money.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.100
You're not my mom, you know.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:55.260
It's chain mail! There's ring mail! Here's plate mail!

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.260
He's so happy, that moron.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.920
I see.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.580
So, this is still technically Abenobashi Shopping Arcade.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.450
Even if it is a bit weird.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.130
I wonder what kinda Great Evil Lord is here?

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.120
Oh, the decisions.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.830
With this and this, I'll be over budget...

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:20.330
...but I can't take this gauntlet off.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.170
And I need this shield here, too.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.570
Oh, and this one here's tough to let go of too.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.160
The decisions!

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.090
Shouldn't he have other stuff to agonize about?

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.820
You seem to be troubled, Miss.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.020
What? Oh...

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.610
I have no place to go home to.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.720
Oh, you're lost.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.330
Then buy the key chain of good luck.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.630
I'll sell it to you cheap.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.620
Oh, do I look mega cool or what?!

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.940
To hell with it! With all of that together...

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.290
God damn it! 600 it is! Rob me blind, why don't you?!

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.200
We have 800 gold pieces.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.660
The theory here is to leave a minimum of 200 for finding a place to stay and stuff like that.

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:26.900
C'mon, the money, the money!

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.140
Arumi! Where d'you go?!

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.650
Hey, what do ya think?!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.570
All of this, only for 600 gold pieces!

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.910
And right now, every customer also gets a high class alligator leather sheath...

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.420
...and an all-purpose Taisho Era Japanese harp...

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.210
...that you can even play while you're taking a bath!

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.170
Ta-da!

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.540
I bought this!

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.620
Bought it? Why?

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:51.090
Oh, I just wanted this one thing.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.250
So, how much was it?

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.760
Would you believe it?! It was exactly 800 gold pieces!

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.510
No!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.230
A knockoff key chain gilded to the hilt cost 800 gold pieces...

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.340
And just like that, we're penniless.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.150
Buying a wooden sword as a souvenir on a school trip...

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.780
...would've still been better than this.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.090
Sure, you say that, but when you're told it's half off the normal price...

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.080
...for the real thing that even the supermodel Christine uses...

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:22.890
Who the heck is that?

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.860
Don't you know? That famous Christine!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.250
Or was it Stephanie?

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.460
Barbara?

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.330
Who?

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.530
I don't know!

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:34.830
That's gotta be fake! Arumi, you got scammed!

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.870
What? Then it wasn't actually half off?

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.310
Was it more like 20% off?

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.540
No, that's not my point.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:42.570
He had on such a shabby hooded cape...

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.650
...really looking the part of "I'm a good-hearted wizard"...

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.770
...and he only gave me 20% off?!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.120
That mister was good! What a tradesman!

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:53.230
A shabby hooded cape?

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.150
Yeah, a mister with long hair and a cane.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.690
Could he have been a sorcerer?!

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.330
Which would make this a magical item?!

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.770
Shoot, I'm getting dizzy.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.860
So, Arumi, what did the guy say about the attributes of this thing?

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:11.590
What?

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.640
That's kind of a secret.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:16.800
Why?

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.150
This is...

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:26.930
What is it?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.260
Here's a freaky-looking lady.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.240
I wonder what's so funny?

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.140
She's weird, don't make eye contact with her.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:54.320
Oh, if we make eye contact, she'll attack us and steal our lunches!

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.500
That's a monkey!

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:59.140
I cannot allow you to advance a single step beyond this point!

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:04.160
Oh, no, we're gonna be going this way anyway, so...

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.460
Please don't mind us.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.100
I see, so you insist on trying to get past me.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.520
We didn't say that.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:11.970
It cannot be helped.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.770
In that case, you must first fight and best me, Mune-mune!

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.370
Fight her breasts?

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:23.300
All right, so you're going to insist on doing this!

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.340
In that case...

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.450
Holy crap!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.990
Arumi, gimme the magical item that we poured our entire savings into!

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:36.210
I'm pretty sure it won't work against her.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:39.190
Take this!

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:47.960
Sasshi!

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.460
Talk about lame.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.270
Oh, he's really dead!

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.510
You can't get out yet!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:01.380
What the heck am I supposed to do?!

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.980
Oh, Hero Sasshi, how could you end up dying?

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.700
Oh, Sasshi's soul, come reside in this body once again.

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.350
Morning.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.280
I see.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.870
I'm slowly beginning to get the hang of the rules in this world.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.660
Quit that! It's depressing!

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:52.370
But it's standard background music.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.100
'Sides, why're you walking in single file when it's just the two of us?!

00:12:57.870 --> 00:12:59.860
You really are a newbie, aren't you?

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:03.740
Each world has its own conventions, you see.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.880
You got killed right off the bat by a Slime!

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.780
Why're you talking like you're some expert?!

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.140
If you're a hero, then walk in front like a real hero!

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:13.980
Say, Arumi...

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:17.160
...why didn't you bring out the magical item for me?

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.830
Like I said, it wouldn't be effective against her.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.520
What kinda magic is that?

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:23.830
Ahem.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.600
At any rate, most importantly, in other words...

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.830
...we most likely absolutely have to defeat the Great Evil Lord to get out of this place.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.440
What the heck? Suddenly taking on an explanatory tone...

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:37.940
Well, you're probably right, but where could the Great Evil Lord be?

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.110
Don't worry! This kind of map generally only has one linear path.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.970
You're not getting past me.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.130
Red Snake?!

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:54.420
Come on!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:57.850
There's a Yellow Snake too.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:01.800
Okay, now you're in the lead. Go out there and fight.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.650
That system is way too old!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.800
No questions asked!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.170
Oh shoot!

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:29.230
Sasshi, can't you at least do a little something?

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:32.600
You just keep standing there like an idiot and getting killed.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:36.230
But if you really think about it, don't I have zero equipment?

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.560
Mini-Boss? We haven't even cleared one map.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.950
Hero, you have done well to make it this far. I'm impressed.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.200
Oh, this is the arbitrary advancement of plot that you get in a lot of crap games.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.750
But you two will die here!

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.560
You two?! Does that mean me, too?!

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.750
How many times have I already died today?!

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:06.500
If we both die here, it'll be "game over", right?

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.000
Die!

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.830
Whoa, wait, stop, that's dangerous!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.140
Hey, lady, what're you doing?!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.310
Prepare to die!

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.450
Sasshi, watch out!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.560
No!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.500
I hate snails! I can't stand snails!

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:46.310
Oh-ho, I see, so this is her weakness.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:45.510
No!

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.260
Why the heck do ya have that on ya?

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:48.260
I hate snails!

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.420
'Cause I'm the daughter of a French cook, of course.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.320
I can't stand snails!

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:52.210
You still wouldn't normally carry snails around.

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:53.370
In that case...

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.450
Here, I've got plenty for ya!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.750
No! Please stop! No!

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.280
There! How's that?! There and there!

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:07.220
All right! Magic!

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.170
Excuse me, Arumi-san?

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.600
Hey, you!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:16.620
Please tell me! Who gave you that key chain?

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:20.340
It wasn't given to me, I bought it. From a mister with long hair.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:23.280
Longinus-san? That sounds like a trump card sort of name!

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:25.110
No, no, this guy with hair that's long...

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.290
That person wouldn't have happened to have...

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:28.960
...looked like this?

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:31.120
Yeah, yeah, he did.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.310
It's him! He is in this town!

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.190
So, which way did he go?!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:38.350
That way. I think.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.980
She left...

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.570
I see! So, that's how the magic works.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.770
No, that's probably not what it was.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:57.950
All right, a dungeon means the Evil Lord is coming up soon.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.200
How the heck can you tell?

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:01.750
The inside of a dungeon is where we're close and yet so far.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:18.000
What a nasty way to cut corners! Is that even allowed?!

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.560
Just never mind it.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.070
Here we go! This is the final decisive battle!

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:26.010
The shopping arcade's, no, the fate of the world and our happiness...

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.740
...is riding on this battle!

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.870
Yeah! I'm getting pumped up, I'm getting pumped up, I'm getting pumped up!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.810
Now, go, Hero Sasshi!

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:35.310
Don't mind me! Now, hurry!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.300
It's a monster!

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:52.900
Okay, good luck!

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.300
What's okay?!

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:57.100
You're just watching from a safe distance!

00:17:57.270 --> 00:18:00.760
It's an honest-to-goodness Great Evil Lord!

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:08.050
Good, good, you're doing great!

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.140
Now, just go for it and we'll clear the game!

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.220
No good! I surrender! I give up!

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.890
I'm sorry! My fault! Forgive me!

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:16.820
There's no way I can win against this thing!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.740
'Sides, I don't have any weapons at all!

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:25.410
Arumi-chan! I'm begging you! The key chain!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.190
Oh, fine.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.920
I wonder if this'll actually help, though?

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.090
Now! Legendary Hero Sasshi!

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.550
Not that I really understand what's going on.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.850
Oh, to hell with it!

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.820
What the heck is this thing?! It's totally useless!

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:04.030
Take a closer look! See?! It's starting to take effect!

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:12.840
What the?! What the?!

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.540
Something weird's starting to happen...

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:19.130
How's this?!

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.220
There, there, there, there, and there!

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:28.730
It's working, it's working!

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:32.980
Say, is this magic...

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.030
The chest's getting larger 'n larger...

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:51.310
Sasshi!

00:19:56.660 --> 00:20:00.170
Oh, the magic's gone.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:06.680
What the heck is this?

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:12.190
I lose, I lose! I'll grant you one wish, anything you want!

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:13.740
What?!

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:15.380
We cleared the game!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.240
Then, for our wish, we want to go home!

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:19.900
Send us back to the world we came from!

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:22.670
I understand!

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.710
What the heck is this?

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:42.470
Really, we should have all sorts of offerings too, but it'll be okay. Probably.

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:44.890
Probably? Is it going to be all right?

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:47.400
You'll be able to get there with this!

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.370
Now, stand there!

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:55.150
Put your hands together!

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.410
Let's see. Like this?

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.350
Don't you start talking that way too.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.340
Close your eyes!

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:06.570
Now, chant it three times, just like you did earlier.

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:09.330
All things extant in this world...

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.500
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:16.170
All things extant in this world...

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:20.000
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.980
All things extant in this world...

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:27.220
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:29.210
Thus shall it be.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:38.530
Are we there?

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.560
Is it okay to open our eyes?

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:42.860
It's night. The stars are so pretty.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:54.110
Are we back?

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:10.450
What the heck is going on?!

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:47.550
Okay, it's the next episode preview.

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:48.890
I'll really do a preview this time.

00:23:48.890 --> 00:23:49.890
Then just do it.

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:50.820
I'm gonna, I'm gonna.

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.860
All right! I'm so happy. I get to do the next episode preview.

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.160
Why're you so happy about something like that?

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:56.930
Why? Arumi, haven't you ever wished upon the stars that you'll get...

00:23:56.930 --> 00:23:59.700
...to do a next episode preview just once in your lifetime?

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:01.440
Of course not. What're you, a moron?

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:04.540
Not a moron! It's something all normal kids would wish for!

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:05.770
You're definitely the only one.

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:07.640
You're so wrong! Everyone does it!

00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:08.740
Well, that doesn't really matter, but...

00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:09.810
It does too matter!

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:12.350
If you don't clear these things up now, later on, they'll...

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:14.210
I think you're out of time.

00:24:14.210 --> 00:24:15.400
What?
